<title>UK: Saudi lifts June crude prices to Europe - trade.</title>
<headline>Saudi lifts June crude prices to Europe - trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has increased the price of its crude oil for European term customers in June by between 15 and 20 cents a barrel, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The state oil giant increased Arab Light by 20 cents to Dated Brent -$2.05 a barrel, Berri Extra Light also by 20 cents to Dated Brent -$1.15 and Arab Heavy by 15 cents to Dated Brent -$4.15, they said.  </p>
<p>Details of the Arab Medium price for June were not immediately available.</p>
<p>--Mark Thompson, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
